      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <p>ALL MEN ARE LIARS.</p>
        <p>Sa writes a Poplar Author.</p>
        <p>Not so bad as that I hope, althou:lh I must admit some men are wickesl liars ; in fact, it's only by accident they ever speak the truth. It is not a lie when Gerslvm, the Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, Oldham-street ; 17, 19, and 21, Hilton-street, Marphester, st ttes that he never attempts to put before the public common new London made rubbilt, more like orange boxes, tor high-class second-band ; it is not a lie when Gershon states that he never attempts to trespass upon his neighbour's b isiness. Why shtmld he ? It only causes a bad feeling. G.-rshon's motto is live and let live. He sticks to the une thing he understands, namely, furnishing. If you can't furnish with a man that understands his business, you cannot do so with men that don't. Gershon has for years cautioned thAl public against buying common new London furniture tor second hand, and he still does so. However distasteful it may be to others. Gershon still takes his stand upon the rock of " Honesty and Justice," which are the 'guiding principles of his business, and 'rum which precepts time nor tide will cause him to recede TERMS OF BUSINEQS. RAILWAY FARR PAID TO - COUNTRY CUST MERS. GOOD: STORED FREE 'I ILL REQUIRED. REMEMBIC:."</p>
        <p>Any lot gtdvertised may be had on the deferred paymen system without any extra charge. Goods exchanged if ra.t satisfactory. Mr. Gershon will nurchare or take in exchange a single article or Jomplete kouses of furniture.</p>
      </div>
