      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-08-01_WidnesExaminer_art0044" n="art0044">
        <p>GERSHON'S UNIVERSAL FURNISHING ARCADE, 44, Oldham-street (next to tholphl Bank). Manchester. Charming Drawing•room lot, in t.erfect condition, con- sisting of hands. me Suite, just been re-covered in one of the most fazhionrible coverings: the chartnitig Cabinet to match, lovely Overinantel, two Tab'es, Carpets and Hug, Fender and Fire Brasses, all complete and ready for fit- ting up. A superior drawing-room wed worth £5 ~delivered for 24 guimas. NO EXTRA. CHARGIe FOR CREDIT. FIVE PER CI- NT ALLOWED FOR PROMPT CASH.</p>
        <p>fIERSHON. THE UNIVERSAL FURNISH- ING CONTRACTOR, 44, Oldham-st., next to the Adelphi B:nk, Manchester.</p>
        <p>FROAI ONE of the ABOVE ADDRESSES. Remarkably handsome solid Walnut Bedroom Suite, consi,ting of full eft, wardrobe with two robing bevelled mirrors reaching from plyrith to cornico. fitted with drawers, cupboa:da, and haoging comwrtments ; magnificent pedes- tal dressing table. fitted with eight drawers in the pedestals and large beveiltd ulnas attach&amp; stipportßd by carved brac- kets ; large size pedestal washstand. fitted With clipboards in the ped-stals ; bedside pedestal with napkin drawer, tiwel rail, and three charming upholstered chairs. The suite is guaranteed solid ttirialghout. Well worth £5O: packed, war- ranted, and delivered for 24 guineas. No extra charge for credit, five per cent. allowed for prompt cash, Gershon, Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, (Wham-street, next to Adelphi Bank, Manchester.</p>
        <p>GER-SHON ALLOWS FIVE PER CENT DISCOUNT FOn PROMP t CASH.</p>
        <p>ANUMBER of Bedroom Suites, just like new, from a hotel, in solid American Walnut, Bur Walnut. Satin Walnut, Olive Wood, Bird's Eye Maple, English Ash, Mahogany, Cyprus., and ther woods. Each suite includes a superior wardrobe well-fitted and plate-glass door. bevelled; dressing table with bevelled glass attached, some enclosed, some open, and some with aide reflectors ; double washstand with marble slab, tile back, and bevelled shaving mirror ; bedside cupboard, chairs, and towel airer ; the prices are 18. 16, 14, 12.10 and 8 guinea the suite, packed and delivered. Each suite is worth double. Five percent. for prompt cash. No extra for credit. Call and inspect them. GERSHON, Universal Furnishing Contractor, 44, Oldham-stteet, next to the Adelpid Bank, Manchester.</p>
        <p>GRAND BARGAIN IN DINING-ROOM SUITE. —All the wo d work is guaranteed solid, spring stuffed, covered in dark grain leather, all in perfect order; the covering is new; price, packed and delivered, £4 18s 6d. OharmitL:t Suite, in saddle bags, all new cover- ing, extra strom: :Mid frames ; grand b-trgain for 5 guineas. Several Sideboards, in various woods at marvellously low prices, with bevelled glass hacks; from £4 10s to £6O. Dining Tables, all sizes and all woods ; from 245. Second-hand Carpets. Rugs, Fenders and- every requisite for complete furnishintz, at GERSHON'S, the UNIVERSAL FURNISH- ING CONTRACTOR. 44, OLDHAM-STREET, next to the</p>
        <p>Adeiphi Panic, MANCHESTER. ALL ARE INVITED TO WALK THROUGH.</p>
        <p>RE SU LT OF UNHAPPY MARRIAGE. DIVORCH PROCBUDINGS' U.. perhaps the most favourable opportunity ever offered to those about furnishing in good style is the present. The furnishing in question has been removed from a very la,ge house in the vicinity of Ply- mouth Grove, and everything was made to order only 14 months ago by one of the best houses in the city. The prices (meted are exactly one-half the cost. Nothing like a full des- cription can be given. Inspection is invited. Firstly. the hall is furnished with a grand dark mahogany Louis Stand end pair chairs to match; price 9 guineas. The dining-room is in solid black walnut of magnificent and uncommon design. To attempt anything like a description would be a waste of time ;to say the leest, it is the most charming and unique, the dining table extending with extra leaves, sup- ported by square legs which, are beautifully carved ; the over- mantel is such that can only be made •Ity workmen of the highest standard ;itis a work of art. Next comss the truly magnificent Suitt , which, of course, are also in solid black walnut, and con- ists of 12 standard Chairs (the price quoted is for six chairs, more can be had if required)., with double- padded sacks, two extra large lounge chsirs, and a grand couch, of large size. sidebo trd alone is worth £5O Os 9d, the whol - ferming a noble lot for high-class dining-room. Price 68 guieeas I have also the carpets, paintings, and engravings from the same room. The drawing room is furnished in the latest style. and surpasses everything for elegance I have ever seen. Firstly, the Curie display cabinet at once strikes you as being a marvel of beauty and workmanship. It possesses all the requirements se such an artistic article Next comes the leindsome music cabinet with face fron and various divisions, lined with plush; two curious shape tables, with fancy cut and carved legs ; the overmanted with diamond-shaped glasses, and recesses for the display ot nick-nacks; lastly, but by no means the least. the truly magnificent suite of double gondola settee, for any part of the room ; two charming easy chairs. four occvional chairs, and two gossipy chairs. All are upholstered in a rich silk tapestry. wills raised fiewers and sprays, and :Wished with silk cord and gimp. It may b- remarked that these fittings are suitable for only a high-class drawing-room. There are in all nine bedrooms, space prevents all being described. The best room of all, I may here state, is suitable for a lady of title or a lord, it cost £l2 and is offered for 60g5. The suite IS simply magnificent, the wood is perteetty solid bright- polished walnut of the choicest quality, the wardrobe is 71t wide, fitted at either end with hanging compartments which are enclosed with brilliant bevelled Vaxhen plate glass of shield shape, bttween the doors are drawers, and ',wove are bay-shaped cupboards, with massive csrved panel', which at once cisplays great dexterity with the chisel. the whole is crowned with a comae of tower like shape,the dressing table Is tift 6itt. wide. p-destal design, and uay-shaped between the pedestals, which are fitted with drawers, the glass, which supported by carved Itracketo, is shield shape and extra large. Next comes the art 61n bay-shaped washstand, with marble slab, tile, and gloss back, about 4ft high, the pedestal towel rail and usholstered chairs forms one of the finest Suites money can buy. There are eight other, bedrooms which contain suites at all prices, some as low as 4 guineas and some at 14, 18, and 25 guineas. The suite from the breaktast room is in saddle bags, price .8 guineas ; dining table, 355; sideboard, £7 15s; twos recesses bookcases. 75s each. Another carved oak bookcase antl,a host of other articles are on view. Carpets, rugs, lenders. 'orna- ments, paintings. china, and glass, all removed to 44, Old- ham-street, Manchester. •</p>
