        <p>PRE MERSEY BEDSTEAD COMPANY. St. James' Street, Knutsford Road, Warrington. 1896—July Ist. £ s. d. Stack-in-Trade on this date, as per Stock Book Fixed and Loose Plant, Trade Utensils, Fixture, and Fittings &amp;c,. as per ditto 1033 11 10 Estimated Expend tura in altering and fitting up the Works 350 0 0 Patent Rights and Registered Designs --- Total £5421 7 5</p>
        <p>Having carefully inspected the Stock-in-Trade. Fixed and Loose Plant, Fixtures. Fittings, and Effects. in and upon the above-named premises as described in the Stock Bi ok of the Company, and having taken into consideration the represen- tations of the Company in reference to he cost incurred in the necessary alterations and fitting up of the Works, and to the value of their pro?. as of japanning whereby they are able to effeat a large saving over the ordinary system of Fire or Gas Stoves, and also taking into account the cost ct registra- tion of designs. I am of opinion that the total silm of Five Thousand Four Hundred and Twenty-One Pounds, Seven Shillings, and Five Pence, as given in the Summary above, is a fair and reasonable value of the whole as on the First day of July, 1896. £5,421 7s. sd. THOMAS SUTTON, Licensed Valuer, Warrington. 10th July, 1896. The books of the concern have been examined by Mr. James Bolton, Public Aeceuntant, Warrington, and the following is a copy of his Certificate ACCOUNTANT'S CERTIFICATIt. 45, Sankey Street, Warrington, 21st July, 1E96. TO THE DIRECTORS OF THE MERSEY BRDSTEAD CO.. LI MIT.SD. Gentlemen, Having examined theb,oks of the Mersey Bedstead Com- pany. and taking the values of the Stock-in-Trade as correct, I beg to certity that, alter cnarging losses in respect of bad debts, the net profits for the six months ending .30th June, 1896, are considerab.y more than sufficient to pay 10 per cent. on the proposed issue of Ordinary Shares, in addition to in- terest on Debenture and Preference Shares. Yours faithfully, JAS. BOLTON, Public Accountant. The purchase price has been fisted by the Vendors at £15,000 payable as to £8,(40 in fully paid up Ordinary Shares of theCempany and the balance in cash. The Vendors have egreed to act as Managing Directors for a period of five years at a remuner ttion to be fixed by the company. and as ordinary Directors for a further period of five years; and they have also entered into an Agreement with the Compaiiy not to carry on or be interested in any competing business during the period of ten years after they respectively shall cease to be Directors. The Vendors will pay all the exr.enses of formation except the cost of preparing, printing and registering the Memoran- dum and Articles of Association ,it the C.impany, which will be paid by the Company. The following Agreemente have been entered into, and all applicants for Shares and Debentures shall be deemed to have had notice of the terms thereof (a) An Agreement dated the 24th day of Jelly. 1896, and made between the said J. Titchett, D Fanshaw. G. Clay, and J. P. Jones of the one part. and William Crampton of the other part, for the sale to the Oimpany of the business and property before described. (b) An agreement dated the 28th day of July, 1896, and made between the said J. Titchett, D. Fanshas, G. Clay, and J. P. Jones of the first part, the said William Crampton of the second part, and the Company of the third part,adopt- ing the last-mentioned Agreement on the part of the Com- pany. In addition to the above-mentioned Agreements there are various trade contracts, and all applicants for shares shall be deemed to have had notice oh these contracts or engagements, and to have waived all right to any particulars thereof, whether under Section 38 of the Companies Act, 1867, or otherwise. Copies of the Memorandum and Articles of Association, and of the above-mentioned Agreements, Valuations, and the Accountant's Certificates, may be inspected at the Offices of the Sol citime to the Company- Applicat one for shares and Debentures must be made on the enclosed forms, and forwarded, together with the deposit, to the Company's Bankers. Allotments will be mile as soon as possible after the list Is closed In cases where no allotment .8 made the deposit will be returned in full, and where the amount allotted is less than that applied for, the surplus will be credited in reduction of the amount payable on allotment. Prospectuses and forms of applicat.on may be obtained from the Bankers. Solicitors, and Auditor, or at the Offices of the Comp my. 29th July, 1896</p>
